<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40159" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quīni</span></b> , ae, a (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>gen. plur.</i>
			quinum, <i><span class="en">Col. 4, 30</span></i>; Pandect. 40, 9, 5: quinorum
			not found), <i>num. distr. adj.</i> [quinque].
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Five each</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quini in lectulis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Pis. 27, 67</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pedes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. G. 3, 73</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ordines,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 7, 23</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">versus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Nep.
					Att. 18, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">milia peditum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 8,
					8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ova pariunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					8, 14, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aureorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					40, 9, 5</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			gen., <i>five</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">minae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ps. 1, 3, 111</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bis quinos silet dies,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 2, 126</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">armenta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 7, 538</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nomina principum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					28, 26</span></i>
			.— In sing.: lex me perdit quina
			vicenaria, i.e. <i>a law invalidating contracts entered
				into before the age of twenty-five</i> (the lex Plaetoria; v.
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Off. 1, 15, 61</span></i>), <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ps.
				1, 3, 69</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scrobes non altiores quino semipede,</span>”
				i. e. <i>two feet and a half</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					17, 11, 16, § 80</span></i>
			.</div>
